# {{ .Name }}

This Python service renders PDF reports for {{ .App }}.
It uses FastAPI, sandboxed Jinja2 templates, and WeasyPrint.

Run the service from the application root with `spinup dev`.
Generate the Go client with `spinup g client`.
Run the tests in a container with `spinup ci test-service {{ .Name }}`.
The tests need the Pango libraries of the Dockerfile.

Run these commands in this directory for local development:

```sh
uv sync --locked
uv run --locked python -m pytest
uv run --locked uvicorn service.main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port {{ .Port }}
```

## The API

`GET /healthz` returns `ok`.
`POST /v1/render` accepts `{"template": "sample", "data": {"title": "March report"}}` and returns `application/pdf`.
The template name selects `service/templates/<template>.html.j2`.
The template reads the object `data`.

| Status | Cause |
|---|---|
| 404 | The template does not exist. |
| 413 | The body is larger than the limit. |
| 422 | The body is not valid, or the template needs a key that `data` does not have. |
| 500 | The render failed, the template loads a URL that is not allowed, or the PDF is larger than 20 MiB. |
| 503 | The render queue is full. The answer has `Retry-After: 5`. |
| 504 | The render took too long. |

Each error is `application/problem+json`.
The service sets no `Content-Disposition`. The Go API sets it with `pdf.Serve`.

## Templates

Add a template as `service/templates/<name>.html.j2`.
The name must match `^[a-z][a-z0-9_]{0,63}$`.
Jinja2 runs in a sandbox with autoescape and `StrictUndefined`.
Do not use the `safe` filter. A test fails when a template uses it.

Put stylesheets, images, and fonts in `service/assets/`.
Load them with a relative URL, such as `<link rel="stylesheet" href="report.css">`.
Load a brand font with `@font-face` from `service/assets/fonts/`.
The renderer loads only `data:` URLs and files in `service/assets/`.
Any other URL makes the render fail.

## Limits

| Variable | Default | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `RENDER_MAX_BODY_BYTES` | 1048576 | The largest request body. |
| `RENDER_TIMEOUT_SECONDS` | 20 | The time for the wait in the queue and the render. |
| `RENDER_MAX_MEMORY_BYTES` | 2147483648 | `RLIMIT_AS` of each render process. |
| `RENDER_CONCURRENCY` | 2 | The renders that run at once. |
| `RENDER_QUEUE_MAX` | 4 | The requests that wait for a render. |

Each render runs in a child process (`python -m service.render_job`).
The service kills the child at the timeout and when its output passes 20 MiB.
The logs hold the template name, the status, and the time. They never hold `data`.

## Tracing

Set `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT` to export traces with OTLP over HTTP.
The span `pdf.render` has the attributes `pdf.template`, `pdf.bytes`, and `pdf.render_ms`.
The FastAPI instrumentation accepts the incoming W3C `traceparent` header.

Keep the project name `service` to preserve the lockfile.
